.TH TAB "1" "October 2026" "tab v1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tab \- tabulate values of a function
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.B tab
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,EXPRESSION\fR [\fI\,FILE\/\fR]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tab
tabulates values of EXPRESSION for each line of input.
EXPRESSION is a Python expression, which may use the variables 'x', 'X', and 'LNUM' to access properties about the current line, and any modules which have been imported by the \fB\-i\fR flag (by defult, the 'math' module will be imported into the global namespace).
Without any options, the entire line will be treated as a single input, and will be replaced in-place by the tabulated value.
By default, each line or field will be converted to an int if it can, then to a float, and otherwise will be treated as a str.
This program will eval() \fIEXPRESSION\fR, so sanitize your inputs to be certain that it does not contain or do any potentially dangerous things.
.PP
The 'x' variable contains the current line, or field, converted to the operating type (see the \fB\-t\fR flag).
.br
The 'X' variable contains the current line as a list, with each field converted to the operating type.
.br
The 'n' variable contains the current line number.
.TP
If no \fFILE\fR is specified on the command line, read from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
Mandatory options to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-append\fR[=\fI\,LOCATION\/\fR]
Append the tabulated value to the line rather than replacing it.
By default, with no \fILOCATION\fR this will insert each tabulated value in the field after the input.
\fILOCATION\fR may be any of '+', '-', or a positive integer.
With '+', the new fields will be appeneded to the end of the line in order of computation.
With '-', the new fields will be inserted just before the field from which it was computed.
With a number, the new fields will be inserted in order after the given field.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-delimiter\fR[=\fI\,DELIMITERS\/\fR]
Use characters in \fIDELIMITERS\fR to separate fields; by default, tabs will be used to separate fields.
If \fIDELIMITERS\fR is not given, separate fields on whitespace.
The first character in \fIDELIMITERS\fR (or ' ' if \fIDELIMITERS\fR is not given) will be used to delimit the output.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-fields\fR[=\fI\,FIELDS\/\fR]
Perform tabulation only for given \fIFIELDS\fR, or if no \fIFIELDS\fR given, for all fields in the line.
Fields are delimited by the \fIDELIMITER\fR characters (see \fB\-d\fR), and may be specified as a comma separated list of field specifications.
All field specifications use 1-indexed numbers, and may be given as
.IP
N: The Nth field, exactly.
.br
N-: The Nth field, and all subsequent fields (actually, from the last field given explicitly to the end of the line).
.br
-M: The first field to the Mth field (actually, from the start of the line to the first explicitly-given field).
.br
N-M: The Nth to Mth fields, inclusive.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-filter\fR
Print only lines for which \fIEXPRESSION\fR evaluates to True.
Most Python objects are True, so it is often useful to explicitly compute False for lines which are to be excluded.
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-headers\fR
Treat the first line of input as containing headers, and print it without attempting to process it.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-import\fR=\fI\,MODULE\fR
Import MODULE to be used by EXPRESSION.
If MODULE does not contain any '.'s, then import into the global namespace.
Otherwise, import normally.
Certain common modules may be abbreviated as a single letter, viz. 'cmath', 'math', 'numpy', 'random', and 'string'.
Only some sanitization is done to prevent nonsense (since this must be eval()'d). Be careful!
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-loose\-errors\fR[=\fI\,VALUE\/\fR]
Do not exit immediately on errors in tabulation.
If no \fIVALUE\fR is given, leave lines or fields which errored unchanged from their original values.
Otherwise, replace them with \fIVALUE\fR.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-loose\-exit\-status\fR
Change the behavior of the exit status.
Normally, the program will exit non-zero if any tabulating errors occur.
This flag will change the behavior such that the program will only exit non-zero if a fatal error is encountered.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Do not print error messages for tabulation errors.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR=\fI\,TYPE\fR
Change the default type to which fields will attempt to be converted, with fields that cannot be converted remaining as str(). 
By default, all fields will attempt to be converted to float(), but \fITYPE\fR may be any type which has already been imported (N.B. this means that \fB\-i\fR and \fB\-t\fR flags are not necessarily order independent).
Certain types may be abbreviated to a single character, viz. 'bytes', 'complex', 'float', 'int', and 'str'.
If 'e' for 'eval' is given, each line or field will be passed to 'eval()' and the result used as the type-converted value.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print a short help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.PP
